# EPIC-XXX Epic Plan

## Design
TODO: interfaces and alternatives

## Security mapping
Map every epic concern to touched or unaffected, with rationale. Boundary booleans reflect this plan, not the epic.

## Accessibility mapping
For UI changes, map acceptance criteria to WCAG 2.2 AA checks: keyboard-only operation, visible focus, semantic HTML/ARIA, labels and errors, contrast, screen-reader output, and zoom/reflow. Obtain independent accessibility signoff before build and again on the reviewed implementation commit.

## Small tasks
One testable behavior per task; exact files, dependencies, QA IDs, RED/GREEN commands, and individual commit. Keep tasks minutes-sized where practical.

## Review evidence
Staff review: correctness, readability, architecture, security, performance. Record every finding in `review_comments`. A finding is resolved only after its fix is committed and the independent code reviewer verifies it on the final `review_commit`. Mandatory AppSec final review follows.
